\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {61}{\ignorespaces Navier--Stokes/FNO2d generalizability $\Delta $RMSE bar chart. Because Navier--Stokes adversarial training requires very large GPU memory and wall-clock time, we did not have enough compute for a complete systematic comparison. Instead, we ran six rounds of Loss 3 adversarial training on the FNO2d dataset and evaluated the trained model against the baseline on broad generalization datasets. Most cases show lower MSE after training, while a few increase, supporting the effectiveness of the method while also showing its practical limitation on memory- and time-intensive problems.}}{86}{figure.61}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:app-g-ns-training-delta-rmse}{{61}{86}{Navier--Stokes/FNO2d generalizability $\Delta $RMSE bar chart. Because Navier--Stokes adversarial training requires very large GPU memory and wall-clock time, we did not have enough compute for a complete systematic comparison. Instead, we ran six rounds of Loss 3 adversarial training on the FNO2d dataset and evaluated the trained model against the baseline on broad generalization datasets. Most cases show lower MSE after training, while a few increase, supporting the effectiveness of the method while also showing its practical limitation on memory- and time-intensive problems}{figure.61}{}}
